        "topic": "Accounting Equation",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2023",
        "question_text": "<p>If assets are $20,000 and liabilities are $8,000, what is the owner's equity?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The accounting equation is: <b>$Assets = Liabilities + Owner's Equity$</b>. Rearranged, <b>$Owner's Equity = Assets - Liabilities$</b>. Thus, $20,000 - $8,000 = <b>$12,000</b>.</p>",
