    "45665": {
        "order_id": 9,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Financial Accounting",
        "topic": "Financial Ratios",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2023",
        "question_text": "<p>If a company's current assets are $50,000, current liabilities are $25,000, and inventory is $10,000, what is the <b>quick ratio</b>?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The quick ratio (acid-test ratio) is calculated as: <b>$(Current Assets - Inventory) / Current Liabilities$</b>. Thus, <b>($50,000 - $10,000) / $25,000 = 1.6</b>.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
